  description="Moving from small-batch to mass production? Here is how to manage your cash flow, inventory, and factory relationships as you grow."
>
  <h2>Growth Stages of an Activewear Brand</h2>
  <p>Scaling a brand requires a shift in mindset—from product development to supply chain management. Understanding the logistical differences between 100 and 10,000 pieces is crucial for survival.</p>
  
  <h3>Stage 1: Validation (100 - 300 Pcs)</h3>
  <p>At this stage, your goal is market fit. Use low MOQs to test different styles and colors. Focus on gathering customer feedback and building a community.</p>

  <h3>Stage 2: Growth (500 - 2,000 Pcs)</h3>
  <p>Once you have a "Hero Product," increase your order volume to reduce unit costs. This is the time to negotiate better fabric prices and optimize your shipping lanes (moving from Air to Sea freight).</p>

  <h3>Stage 3: Mass Market (5,000 - 10,000+ Pcs)</h3>
  <p>Mass production requires advanced quality control and inventory management. You'll likely need to implement a 3PL (Third Party Logistics) provider to handle the fulfillment volume.</p>

  <h3>Fitclo: Your Partner in Every Stage</h3>
  <p>Fitclo can discuss stock trials and custom production as separate routes. Selected ready-stock styles may support a 20-piece-per-style trial after inventory confirmation; OEM/ODM usually requires 150–250 pcs per style per color, depending on the project.</p>
</GuideLayout>
